  "articleBody": "Remodeling a rental property can be a great way to boost its value and appeal, but there are definitely some pitfalls to watch out for. One of the biggest mistakes is overspending on upgrades that just don't fit the neighborhood or tenant expectations. You don't want to put in top-tier finishes in a market that's looking for good value. Another common misstep is skipping a solid profitability review; always ask yourself if this investment will truly pay off. It’s also easy to underestimate the disruption a renovation can cause, especially if you have existing tenants. Planning for that disruption, including clear communication and scheduling, is key. And trust me, hidden damage is a real thing! Failing to account for potential structural issues or liability exposure can lead to big headaches and unexpected costs down the line. To make sure you’re making the right choices, think about the return on investment, how durable your choices are, and how they’ll affect vacancy rates. Sometimes bringing in a professional helps you spot these issues early and keeps your project on track and on budget.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
